  "summary": "Allow `SignPSBTInput` to accept valid 65-byte Taproot signatures ending in `SIGHASH_ALL` when neither `PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE` nor an explicit sighash parameter is set. Previously, unset sighash types defaulted strictly to 64-byte `SIGHASH_DEFAULT` signatures, causing existing 65-byte `SIGHASH_ALL` signatures to fail validation.",
  "problem": "When processing Taproot inputs without an explicit sighash type, `SignPSBTInput` assumed `SIGHASH_DEFAULT` and rejected valid 65-byte `SIGHASH_ALL` signatures, preventing such PSBTs from being further signed or finalized.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes #36507: 'PSBT: SignPSBTInput rejects valid 65-byte taproot script signatures when PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE is absent'",
    "PR description: 'Its check of existing signatures then rejected every 65-byte taproot signature, so a PSBT holding a valid SIGHASH_ALL signature could be neither finalized nor signed further.'"
